        <body>
            <div xml:id="d245">

                <pb facs="0541" n="417" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg417"/>

                <head>No. 241.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pomeroy to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-07-23"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 23, 1881</date>.
                        (Received August 6.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 495.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the dispatch No. 483, dated
                    June 23, 1881, addressed by General Noyes to the Department of State, and
                    relating to revoking by the French Government the prohibitory pork decree, I
                    have the honor to transmit herewith a copy of the answer of Mr. B. St. Hilaire,
                    together with a translation.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>G. P. POMEROY.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d245-a1.xml" xpointer="d245-a1"/>
            </div>
